course: dictionary
lesson: 3147
title: Words for embarrassing moments
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Embarrassing describes something that makes you feel shy, silly or uncomfortable in front of other people. The clue is "in front of other people": you feel embarrassed when others can see or hear you.
explain: «Family parties are loud, embarrassing and great, often all at once.» Here embarrassing means that some moments at the party make people feel awkward, even though the party is also fun. Check your meaning by swapping in a word like awkward: "loud, awkward and great" still makes sense.
explain: Some phrases show embarrassment. «An embarrassing moment» is a time that makes you squirm. «How embarrassing!» is what someone says when they see something awkward happen. «Some phrases ... "I dropped a clanger" for an embarrassing mistake» shows that a clanger is a mistake that makes you feel embarrassed.
fact: Embarrassing means making you feel shy, silly or uncomfortable in front of other people.
fact: Embarrassing things happen to everyone, like falling over or forgetting your lines in a play, and they are soon forgotten.
fact: Sharing embarrassing photos of other people online is unkind, and it can be bullying.
fact: «Cringe» is slang that means embarrassing.
fact: "Dropped a clanger" (UK slang) means made an embarrassing mistake.
exercise: «Falling over in the playground in front of everyone was so embarrassing.» What does embarrassing mean? | *Makes you feel shy, silly or uncomfortable in front of others | Makes you feel very brave and proud | Makes you very tired | Makes a loud noise
exercise: Ruby says, «That was so cringe!» What does cringe mean? | Very hungry | Excellent | Wet and grey | *Embarrassing
exercise: Jamie says, "I dropped a clanger" after giving the wrong answer. What does it mean? | Won a prize for speaking well | Dropped a heavy bag | Lost his way home | *Made an embarrassing mistake
test: "Sharing embarrassing photos of a friend online without asking is" | Kind and fun | A way to make new friends | *Unkind, and it can be bullying | Something teachers never see
test: What does «an embarrassing moment» mean? | A quiet time in the library | A time when you win a race | A time when the sun shines | *A time that makes you feel shy or silly in front of others
exam: Which sentence uses embarrassing correctly? | *Walking into the wrong classroom in front of everyone was embarrassing. | The cake was embarrassing and sweet. | The rain was embarrassing and wet. | We went to the park to be embarrassing.
